        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rosario Castellanos, Arthur Hailey\n- Places: Centro Cultural Bella Época, Rosario Castellanos bookshop\n- Products: Airport\n- Topics: Literature, bookstores\n\nFacts:\n- Rosario Castellanos Figueroa was born on 25 May 1925 and died on 7 August 1974.\n- Arthur Hailey was born on 5 April 1920 and died on 24 November 2004.\n- Rosario Castellanos Figueroa was a Mexican poet and author.\n- Arthur Hailey was a British-Canadian novelist known for plot-driven storylines set in various industries.\n- Airport is a bestselling novel by British-Canadian writer Arthur Hailey.\n- Centro Cultural Bella Época includes the Rosario Castellanos bookshop.\n- The Rosario Castellanos bookshop is claimed to be the largest bookshop in Latin America.\n- The Rosario Castellanos bookshop carries more than 35 thousand different titles and includes a children’s area, a coffee shop, and reading facilities.",
